@startuml physical-view
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title AISafe - Physical view (deployment on Proxmox + k3s)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam nodeFontStyle bold

actor "Client\n(Postman, browser)" as client
cloud "Virtual IPs (MetalLB)\n.25 aircraft-maintenance · .26 airports-routes\n.27 flight-ops · .28 login" as vips

node "Proxmox host" as px {
  node "VM k3s1 · 192.168.124.43" as n1 {
    component "entry (Envoy)" as e1
    rectangle "aircraft-maintenance-0 :8081\nairports-routes-0 :8082\nflight-ops-0 :8083\nlogin-0 :8085" as p1
    database "own disk per replica\n(H2 files)" as d1
  }
  node "VM k3s2 · .44" as n2 {
    component "entry (Envoy)" as e2
    rectangle "aircraft-maintenance-1\nairports-routes-1\nflight-ops-1\nlogin-1" as p2
    database "own disks (H2)" as d2
  }
  node "VM k3s3 · .45" as n3 {
    component "entry (Envoy)" as e3
    rectangle "aircraft-maintenance-2\nairports-routes-2\nflight-ops-2\nlogin-2" as p3
    database "own disks (H2)" as d3
  }
}

client --> vips : HTTPS :443
vips --> e1 : announced by one VM
vips ..> e2
vips ..> e3
e1 --> p1 : a ready replica (HTTP)
e2 --> p2
e3 --> p3
e1 -[dashed,norank]-> p2 : or one on another VM
p1 --> d1
p2 --> d2
p3 --> d3
p1 <-[dashed,norank]-> p2 : peer to peer
p2 <-[dashed,norank]-> p3 : peer to peer
e1 -[hidden]right- e2
e2 -[hidden]right- e3

legend bottom
  k3s with the control plane on the 3 VMs: any one can be lost.
  One replica of each service per VM (StatefulSets: stable names, own disk).
  A virtual IP moves to another VM when its VM is lost.
  The vigia turns a stopped VM back on (Proxmox API) and moves the replicas
  of a VM that does not come back; a frozen VM is restarted by the watchdog.
  Node ports 30810-30812, 30820-30822, 30830-30832: one replica directly (tests).
endlegend
@enduml
